 - libr3's native gfx1100 prefill reads the same LDS layout `storeVi8` writes; only the selftest rewrite gained the
   b16i8 split-row line.
 
+### ENG06 decode scale-load optimisation (hardware A/B pending)
+
+Only the `fetchVi8` decode path changes. At TILE 16 and a 32-dimension
+scale group, four lanes in a wave read the same token's scale: lanes
+`kp`, `kp + 8`, `kp + 16`, and `kp + 24`. One elected lane loads the
+f16 value and `__shfl` distributes its exact 16-bit representation;
+other scale-group sizes keep the original direct read. The int8 code
+loads, conversion, f16 multiply, LDS staging, cache row bytes, writer and
+fused gate/quantiser remain unchanged. This is a mechanics-only candidate
+for ENG06, not yet a demonstrated GPU speedup or bit-identity proof.
+Device-independent package tests cover the access mapping and anchors;
+hardware kernel correctness/bit identity and A/B remain required.
+
 ### Promotion record
 
